        "title": "Add CLI product funnel telemetry and run conversion tracking",
        "summary": "The Freebuff CLI now emits `PRODUCT_FUNNEL_STEP` analytics events for user journey stages from launch through turn completion, gated behind the `IS_FREEBUFF` constant. A new `createCliRunFunnel` state machine in the CLI tracks dispatch, start, and response events to classify a run as succeeded, failed, or cancelled based on whether useful root output was produced. The `createRunConfig` utility exposes optional `observeEvent` and `observeChunk` hooks that pipe SDK stream events to this funnel logic without interfering with the agent loop, while a strict Zod schema in the common package rejects payloads containing prompts, paths, or auth identifiers.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "operators",
        "evidence": "The diff adds `common/src/constants/product-funnel.ts` defining `PRODUCT_FUNNEL_EVENT` and a Zod schema, introduces `cli/src/utils/cli-product-funnel.ts` and `cli/src/utils/cli-run-funnel.ts`, and modifies `cli/src/utils/create-run-config.ts` to accept optional `observeEvent` and `observeChunk` callbacks that forward SDK events to the funnel state machine.",
